# VegaAM build-time credentials (copy to `.env.local`, never commit `.env.local`)
#
# These values are OPTIONAL. The open-source VegaAM build ships WITHOUT a
# built-in Last.fm key pair: Last.fm's API terms expect every application to
# identify itself with its own credentials, so the user creates a Last.fm API
# application and enters the key pair in Settings -> Accounts.
#
# If you build a PRIVATE release for your own users and want the key pair
# baked into the binary, set them here:
#
#   VEGAAM_LASTFM_API_KEY     - public half of the Last.fm application key pair
#   VEGAAM_LASTFM_API_SECRET  - private half of the Last.fm application key pair
#
# `build/build.mjs` injects them into the main-process bundle only. The
# renderer bundles never see them.
#
# A shared secret that was published publicly is revoked: `npm run dist`
# refuses to build with it. Rotate the secret at Last.fm first, then put the
# new values here.
#
# These values are embedded in the shipped application and can be extracted
# from it. They are an application identity, not a user credential - the user
# session key is what VegaAM stores in the operating system keychain.

VEGAAM_LASTFM_API_KEY=
VEGAAM_LASTFM_API_SECRET=
